        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1c4b329d-63c7-50fe-9850-cf2a5829b9b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Tull, Todd Phillips, Daniel Goldberg, Jon Lucas, Scott Moore\n- Companies: Legendary Entertainment, Warner Bros., Universal Studios, Toho\n- Products: The Hangover, MonsterVerse\n- Concepts: film production, media franchise, shared fictional universe\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Tull was born in 1970 and is an American businessman and film producer.\n- Legendary Entertainment was founded by Thomas Tull in 2000.\n- In 2005, Legendary Entertainment concluded an agreement with Warner Bros. to co-produce and co-finance films.\n- The Hangover is a 2009 American comedy film directed by Todd Phillips, co-produced with Daniel Goldberg, and written by Jon Lucas and Scott Moore.\n- The Hangover follows Phil Wenneck, Stu Price, Alan Garner, and Doug Billings as they travel to Las Vegas for a bachelor party before Doug Billings's marriage.\n- In 2014, Legendary Entertainment began a similar film co-production arrangement with Universal Studios.\n- The MonsterVerse is an American media franchise and shared fictional universe centered on monster films featuring Godzilla and King Kong.\n- The MonsterVerse is distributed by Warner Bros. and produced by Legendary Entertainment in partnership with Toho for the Godzilla films.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6544cd49-7628-5adf-854b-4429e06da93b",
        "text": "Page: Thomas Tull. Sentence: Thomas Tull (born 1970) is an American businessman and film producer.\nPage: The Hangover. Sentence: The Hangover is a 2009 American comedy film directed by Todd Phillips, co-produced with Daniel Goldberg, and written by Jon Lucas and Scott Moore.\nPage: The Hangover. Sentence: It tells the story of Phil Wenneck, Stu Price, Alan Garner, and Doug Billings, who travel to Las Vegas for a bachelor party to celebrate Doug's impending marriage.\nPage: Legendary Entertainment. Sentence: The company was founded by Thomas Tull in 2000 and in 2005, concluded an agreement to co-produce and co-finance films with Warner Bros., and began a similar arrangement with Universal Studios in 2014.\nPage: MonsterVerse. Sentence: The MonsterVerse is an American media franchise and shared fictional universe that is centered on a series of monster films featuring Godzilla and King Kong, distributed by Warner Bros. and produced by Legendary Entertainment in partnership with Toho (for the \"Godzilla\" films).",
